.gsd/milestones/M001/slices/S01/tasks/T01-SUMMARY.md:29:- `triggarr/config.py`: config generation, loading, migration, backups, and `.migrated` marker creation all operate relative to the supplied `config_path`. This is runtime-configurable behavior.
.gsd/milestones/M001/slices/S01/tasks/T01-SUMMARY.md:30:- `triggarr/web/routes.py`: settings, auth, instance add/remove, API-key, and security write paths use `request.app.state.config_path` and `request.app.state.state_path`, preserving the startup-provided location. The dashboard and dismiss-migration route use `CONFIG_DIR / ".migrated"`; in production this matches the env-derived config path, while path-injected tests patch `CONFIG_DIR`. I did not classify this as a runtime bug because production startup derives both `CONFIG_DIR` and `config_path` from the same `TRIGGARR_CONFIG_DIR` value.
